WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Farmers are increasingly burdened
by the high costs to market,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.400
finding it difficult to compete
with large monocrop farms.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.600
Consumers are also burdened
by centralized distribution,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.200
with longer routes to market,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.900
increased waste, and goods that
need additives to maintain freshness.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.400
A farmer's market offers an alternative,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.500
but it requires time and fees

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.200
that don't necessarily offset
the relative sales volume.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.000
Through FarmerDrop, the supply chain
is completely decentralized.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.000
Farmers set their own fair prices
and deliver to nearby HostDrop locations.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.400
Members pre-order their goods

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.100
and pick up within their neighborhood.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.000
Small and large farmers are now
on the same playing field,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.680
with full flexibility to adapt
to their local community needs.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.160
The FarmerDrop model provides a significant
reduction in distribution costs,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.800
resulting in savings to all users.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.080
As FarmerDrop grows,
the real magic happens.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.000
Neighborhoods transform into marketplaces,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.920
members become small-scale producers,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.840
and communities convert from being
big-chain dependent

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.520
to sovereign value creators.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.920
FarmerDrop works across all regions,

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.920
putting autonomy back into the hands
of each and every community.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.500
Join us on this journey

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.840
at FarmerDrop.com.
